issue.body:
Using the latest OF from Github.

I don't know which version of XCode, OF, or macOS created this problem.

Here's a simple example that should take 4 seconds for a line to walk across the screen from left to right:

```c++
#include "ofMain.h"

class ofApp : public ofBaseApp {
public:
    void setup() {
        ofSetVerticalSync(true);
        ofBackground(0);
    }
    void update() {
    }
    void draw() {
        ofDrawRectangle(ofGetFrameNum() % 240, 0, 1, 240);
    }
};

int main() {
    ofSetupOpenGL(240, 240, OF_WINDOW);
    ofRunApp(new ofApp());
}
```

Instead, it runs much faster, similar to how apps would run without a framerate limit when they are in the background/not in focus.
